From b2e70249806a17737a3359a3345cc213f6685516 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:36:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/24] l2r-local: step D (R2, rest): the tests of the reviewed
 patch that the pull requests left out

The owned handle of `Nat` and `Int` at polyffi type arguments (local
patch R2) went upstream as #824 (the handle, reussir_rt::rcgmp::Mpz),
#843 (the polymorphic FFI spells `Nat` and `Int` as `Mpz`) and #845 (the
tests of std's collections and of the edge cases), with shorter tests
than the reviewed patch. The code is the same. This keeps the reviewed
patch's tests that none of them has:
- a reussir-core unit test of the spellings: a type argument and a
  generic instantiated at `Nat` are the owned handle; a `Nat` the
  signature declares stays the raw handle, which the wrapper releases
  after the body (semi.rs);
- frontend/bigint_ffi_generic.rr's two more properties (six, not four)
  and its driver;
- frontend/bigint_ffi_edge.rr's membership checks of a Rust set of
  `Int`s across signs, and its fuller header (its sanitizer run is
  #845's sanitizer/bigint-ffi-std-asan.rr).
